  "solution": "The logic followed here is :\n\nLogic: **(1st number)² × [-(1st number ÷ 2 - 1)] = 2nd number.**\n\nNow,\n\n10 : -400\n\n→ (10)2 × [-(10 ÷ 2 - 1)]\n\n→ 100 × [-(5 - 1)]\n\n→ 100 × -4 = -400.\n\n6 : -72\n\n→ (6)2 × [-(6 ÷ 2 - 1)]\n\n→ 36 × [-(3 - 1)]\n\n→ 36 × -2 = 72.\n\nSimilarly, for **4 : ?**\n\n**→ (4)2 × [-(4 ÷ 2 - 1)]**\n\n**→ 16 × [-(2 - 1)]**\n\n**→ 16 × 1 = 16.**\n\nHence, the correct answer is** \"Option 1\".**",
